<title>UK: June gas oil delivery 136,000 tonnes - IPE.</title>
<headline>June gas oil delivery 136,000 tonnes - IPE.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>The delivery against the expired June IPE gas oil contract will be 1,360 lots, or 136,000 tonnes, the IPE said.  </p>
<p>Dealers had been expecting a far smaller volume to be delivered with forecasts oscillating around the 50,000 tonne mark.</p>
<p>Last month, some 97,100 tonnes of gas oil was delivered into the May contract.</p>
<p>The June contract stood at $162.25 a tonne when it expired at 1100 GMT.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom, +44 171 542 7714.</p>
</text>
